            <ArticleTitle>Acute celiac trunk thrombosis revealed by biliary peritonitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1199-201</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diii.2015.04.010</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S2211-5684(15)00189-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute thrombosis of the celiac trunk is a very uncommon condition, which is a life-threatening emergency. The clinical presentation is highly variable depending on the extent of the ischemic territory. We report a case of biliary peritonitis related to an acute thrombosis of the celiac trunk. This case highlights the role of abdominal computed tomography in the diagnosis of acute upper abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
